      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T09:45:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve debated with myself several times whether I should take the time to remove this discrepancy. Currently, Rust uses these locks:\n\n* A mutex on process. Used only to protect the collection of nodes.\n* A spinlock on process. This also protects nodes owned by the process.\n* A spinlock on thread. This is separate from the process.\n\nI believe this exists due to a historical accident: the `LockedBy` utility needed for having a struct be protected by a lock in a different struct was probably not implemented yet when locks were added to threads.",
      "parentUuid": "b10b8add_0b99ddfc",
      "revId": "c0bf3401d8ad68c748aa0c67ef2ed634bafbfd7e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
